WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:02.840
<i>"To my sister, Satsuki:</i>

00:00:03.100 --> 00:00:06.800
<i>I was happy to see you at the Great 
Cherry Blossom Banquet the other day.</i>

00:00:06.800 --> 00:00:10.260
<i>I'm glad that you still aspire 
to become a priestess.</i>

00:00:10.810 --> 00:00:11.960
<i>Also..."</i>

00:01:39.700 --> 00:01:49.040
<b>Konohana Kitan</b>

00:01:49.880 --> 00:01:54.050
<b>Episode 4 
Raft Bridge of Dreams</b>

00:02:24.820 --> 00:02:26.530
What was that scream?

00:02:26.530 --> 00:02:27.990
Nacchan, you idiot!

00:02:27.990 --> 00:02:28.590
Pervert!

00:02:28.590 --> 00:02:30.620
What have you done to me?!

00:02:31.310 --> 00:02:33.320
What are you even talking about?

00:02:33.500 --> 00:02:36.170
It's way too early in the morning for this.

00:02:36.170 --> 00:02:38.630
Take responsibility for this!

00:02:39.580 --> 00:02:42.390
We've been sleeping in the same 
room together every day.

00:02:42.390 --> 00:02:44.900
It's obviously your child!

00:02:44.900 --> 00:02:45.930
Wait, wait, wait!

00:02:46.150 --> 00:02:48.330
I mean, I'll take responsibility, but...

00:02:48.330 --> 00:02:49.180
You will?!

00:02:49.180 --> 00:02:51.010
No, that's not even the problem.

00:02:52.990 --> 00:02:54.560
An egg?

00:02:55.930 --> 00:02:57.780
It won't come off.

00:02:58.730 --> 00:03:00.480
What kind of egg is that?

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:02.270
We can find out if we let it hatch.

00:03:02.620 --> 00:03:04.990
In any case, you can't work like that.

00:03:04.990 --> 00:03:06.810
Y-You can't be serious!

00:03:06.810 --> 00:03:09.110
Do you really plan to attend 
to guests like that?

00:03:09.110 --> 00:03:13.290
Why should I have to sit 
on this mystery egg?

00:03:13.670 --> 00:03:16.000
Hang in there until it weans off of you.

00:03:16.380 --> 00:03:19.920
Besides, Ren, whatever this egg is,

00:03:19.920 --> 00:03:23.800
if it grew inside of you, 
it's as good as ours.

00:03:26.950 --> 00:03:29.710
Oh, Ren's taking the day off?

00:03:29.710 --> 00:03:30.680
Yes.

00:03:30.680 --> 00:03:33.290
She's in bed, saying she has a bellyache.

00:03:33.290 --> 00:03:36.560
<i>I hate how she does it so naturally.</i>

00:03:37.220 --> 00:03:39.290
<i>Poor Ren, too.</i>

00:03:39.940 --> 00:03:42.330
I'm going to work hard 
to fill in for Ren-chan.

00:03:42.330 --> 00:03:44.240
For the baby she's carrying, too.

00:03:44.240 --> 00:03:45.020
Yeah.

00:03:45.250 --> 00:03:47.400
But don't say that to anyone else.

00:03:48.010 --> 00:03:48.990
Satsuki!

00:03:48.990 --> 00:03:50.370
Perfect timing.

00:03:52.200 --> 00:03:57.110
This gentleman here saw the Great 
Cherry Blossom Banquet the other day.

00:03:57.780 --> 00:03:59.170
I see.

00:03:59.170 --> 00:04:05.320
That priestess, Hiiragi, who was dancing 
in the middle, was spectacular.

00:04:05.320 --> 00:04:06.970
Do you know of her?

00:04:06.970 --> 00:04:08.540
Of course I do.

00:04:08.540 --> 00:04:10.180
Hiiragi-san is Satsuki's older sis—

00:04:11.640 --> 00:04:13.220
Are you okay?

00:04:11.850 --> 00:04:13.220
Excuse me.

00:04:13.480 --> 00:04:15.930
Did I say something wrong?

00:04:17.900 --> 00:04:20.530
There's a history between her and her sister.

00:04:20.780 --> 00:04:23.610
It's something we may never understand.

00:04:37.010 --> 00:04:38.370
Where am I?

00:04:39.230 --> 00:04:40.240
Who are you?

00:04:41.760 --> 00:04:43.010
Nacchan.

00:04:43.360 --> 00:04:46.210
Why are you dressed so silly?

00:04:46.210 --> 00:04:47.970
It's over between us, Ren.

00:04:48.800 --> 00:04:51.300
I'm actually a prince of the stars.

00:04:51.700 --> 00:04:54.650
So I can't stay here any longer.

00:04:55.700 --> 00:04:57.600
Goodbye, Ren.

00:04:57.600 --> 00:04:59.180
No! Wait!

00:04:59.490 --> 00:05:02.390
I'll eat your carrots if 
you hate them so much.

00:05:02.390 --> 00:05:04.950
I won't get mad at you 
for tossing in your sleep.

00:05:04.950 --> 00:05:08.580
So please, don't go anywhere!

00:05:11.510 --> 00:05:12.740
Don't worry.

00:05:14.340 --> 00:05:16.300
I'm not going anywhere.

00:05:19.230 --> 00:05:20.040
Ren!

00:05:20.350 --> 00:05:21.310
Ren!

00:05:22.900 --> 00:05:24.450
Are you okay, Ren?

00:05:24.450 --> 00:05:25.970
You were having a nightmare.

00:05:29.380 --> 00:05:31.270
Hey, the egg fell—

00:05:31.270 --> 00:05:32.840
How are you feeling, Ren?

00:05:37.480 --> 00:05:39.490
Why is it stuck to me?

00:05:39.490 --> 00:05:40.970
Damn it! It won't come off.

00:05:40.970 --> 00:05:44.540
It seemed to come off Ren-chan by itself 
after she was asleep for a while.

00:05:44.540 --> 00:05:45.380
That's crazy!

00:05:45.380 --> 00:05:48.450
I can't skip work for this nonsense!

00:05:46.500 --> 00:05:48.310
Stop!

00:05:48.600 --> 00:05:51.530
You need to treat your body 
better when you're expecting.

00:05:51.530 --> 00:05:54.490
That body doesn't belong to you 
alone anymore, you know.

00:05:54.490 --> 00:05:56.900
Quit being so suggestive!

00:05:56.900 --> 00:05:59.620
What's going on? It's awfully noisy in here.

00:06:01.520 --> 00:06:02.830
I see.

00:06:02.830 --> 00:06:03.810
All right.

00:06:03.810 --> 00:06:05.550
Let's give it a night and see what happens.

00:06:06.500 --> 00:06:09.380
Take the night off, Satsuki.

00:06:10.910 --> 00:06:14.090
Hey, tell me when you go into labor.

00:06:14.090 --> 00:06:16.090
Stop saying things like that!

00:06:16.810 --> 00:06:19.510
Hey, Ren, which room is this dinner for?

00:06:17.410 --> 00:06:19.510
<i>Why did this happen to me?</i>

00:06:20.040 --> 00:06:21.600
The Akebono room.

00:06:21.600 --> 00:06:24.320
I just served that room.

00:06:24.320 --> 00:06:26.810
Which room is it, then?

00:06:28.090 --> 00:06:29.560
Oh! I'm sorry!

00:06:28.900 --> 00:06:30.520
I'm way too distracted to sleep.

00:06:29.560 --> 00:06:30.540
Are you okay?

00:06:30.540 --> 00:06:32.340
I'll bring a rag.

00:06:32.340 --> 00:06:33.410
Look out!

00:06:34.140 --> 00:06:36.230
I'm sorry!

00:06:34.140 --> 00:06:38.320
Just what is your purpose?

00:06:37.330 --> 00:06:38.980
Are you okay?

00:06:46.780 --> 00:06:48.050
Satsuki.

00:06:49.670 --> 00:06:52.180
Look. It's my new kimono.

00:06:52.180 --> 00:06:53.320
Do I look good?

00:06:53.880 --> 00:06:56.810
<i>You're dauntless and good-looking,</i>

00:06:56.810 --> 00:07:00.350
<i>and you make everyone happy, 
like a large flower.</i>

00:07:00.960 --> 00:07:04.300
We'll send Hiiragi to serve at Konohanatei.

00:07:04.300 --> 00:07:09.560
But dear, everyone expects 
Hiiragi to become a priestess.

00:07:09.560 --> 00:07:10.770
Indeed.

00:07:10.770 --> 00:07:13.490
Then let's send Satsuki instead.

00:07:15.450 --> 00:07:17.410
What do you think, Satsuki?

00:07:19.450 --> 00:07:20.760
I...

00:07:21.190 --> 00:07:24.800
<i>If it doesn't matter either way, 
they'd rather have my sister become one.</i>

00:07:25.110 --> 00:07:26.750
<i>That's what everyone wanted.</i>

00:07:27.080 --> 00:07:27.920
<i>So...</i>

00:07:28.140 --> 00:07:29.200
So?

00:07:29.860 --> 00:07:32.040
So you're telling me you gave me your spot?

00:07:32.350 --> 00:07:36.180
You hid yourself away, 
and now you're blaming me for it?

00:07:36.410 --> 00:07:37.470
<i>No.</i>

00:07:38.160 --> 00:07:40.590
It doesn't matter what anyone else thinks.

00:07:40.900 --> 00:07:42.810
<i>It wouldn't matter what I said.</i>

00:07:42.810 --> 00:07:46.080
<i>I would just hurt you and our parents.</i>

00:07:46.920 --> 00:07:49.270
How do <i>you</i> feel?

00:07:49.730 --> 00:07:53.520
I could never bring myself to say this.

00:07:54.210 --> 00:07:58.830
If it didn't matter which of us would become 
a priestess, if it didn't matter who,

00:07:59.490 --> 00:08:01.870
then why couldn't it have been me?

00:08:02.680 --> 00:08:03.700
What the...

00:08:06.150 --> 00:08:09.160
It <i>does</i> matter who.

00:08:10.020 --> 00:08:12.560
It has to be you, Satsuki-chan.

00:08:13.010 --> 00:08:15.400
We need you. Konohanatei needs you.

00:08:15.400 --> 00:08:17.270
You're needed here.

00:08:18.260 --> 00:08:20.780
It can't be anyone else.

00:08:25.220 --> 00:08:26.390
Satsuki-chan!

00:08:26.500 --> 00:08:27.750
Satsuki-chan!

00:08:27.940 --> 00:08:29.310
Satsuki-chan!

00:08:29.310 --> 00:08:30.920
Are you all right?

00:08:30.920 --> 00:08:32.650
You were having a nightmare.

00:08:33.700 --> 00:08:34.850
Yuzu...

00:08:34.850 --> 00:08:36.290
I'm fine.

00:08:36.290 --> 00:08:37.730
I was having a dream.

00:08:41.910 --> 00:08:42.990
The egg...

00:08:43.240 --> 00:08:44.230
What's going on?

00:08:55.450 --> 00:08:56.450
What is that?

00:08:56.840 --> 00:08:58.300
<b>Konohanatei</b>

00:08:56.840 --> 00:08:58.300
<b>Konohanatei</b>

00:08:58.300 --> 00:09:00.460
Is it a pig?

00:09:00.460 --> 00:09:02.400
It has fur, though.

00:09:02.400 --> 00:09:04.260
It's a melon boy, then.

00:09:02.400 --> 00:09:06.730
<i>[An "uribou" is a wild boar piglet; the compound 
consists of the kanji for "melon" and "boy"]</i>

00:09:04.490 --> 00:09:06.730
Your name is Urinosuke.

00:09:06.730 --> 00:09:09.490
I'm just glad that's all over.

00:09:09.820 --> 00:09:11.560
Can you get back to work right away?

00:09:11.560 --> 00:09:12.700
Sure.

00:09:12.700 --> 00:09:14.030
Thank goodness.

00:09:14.030 --> 00:09:17.150
Work just doesn't get done without you around.

00:09:17.150 --> 00:09:18.730
Kiri-san's so useless.

00:09:18.730 --> 00:09:20.020
Well, <i>sorry</i>, jeez.

00:09:20.020 --> 00:09:21.360
Ow, ow, ow!

00:09:23.490 --> 00:09:25.810
<i>Come say hi sometimes.</i>

00:09:26.200 --> 00:09:30.300
<i>I'd like to meet your friends, too.</i>

00:09:30.970 --> 00:09:32.460
<i>See you soon.</i>

00:09:32.810 --> 00:09:33.710
<i>Hiiragi.</i>

00:09:35.200 --> 00:09:39.730
By the way, were you having 
a bad dream or something?

00:09:39.730 --> 00:09:40.640
Yeah.

00:09:40.640 --> 00:09:44.080
I think it started off as a nightmare, 
but I can't remember.

00:09:44.080 --> 00:09:46.170
It turned into a good dream, and...

00:09:46.440 --> 00:09:49.950
Me, too. I can't remember 
the bad part, either.

00:09:49.950 --> 00:09:54.160
Good thing it was the bad part you forgot.

00:09:54.440 --> 00:09:57.020
So what kind of good dream was it?

00:10:01.560 --> 00:10:02.400
I forget.

00:10:03.010 --> 00:10:04.190
But you just said...

00:10:04.190 --> 00:10:04.620
Drop it!

00:10:04.620 --> 00:10:05.860
I said I forgot!

00:10:06.140 --> 00:10:07.490
Sorry.

00:10:08.550 --> 00:10:13.850
Speaking of dreams, isn't there 
a beast god that eats nightmares?

00:10:11.420 --> 00:10:14.420
<b>Baku</b>

00:10:14.420 --> 00:10:16.620
What was it called again?

00:10:16.620 --> 00:10:17.630
Dunno.

00:10:24.730 --> 00:10:25.710
It's me, Yuzu.

00:10:25.710 --> 00:10:27.690
I'm back from shopping.

00:10:28.180 --> 00:10:29.970
Yuzu! Thank goodness you're here!

00:10:29.970 --> 00:10:31.760
Make this baby stop crying.

00:10:35.320 --> 00:10:38.110
Which guest does it belong to?

00:10:38.110 --> 00:10:39.460
There, there.

00:10:38.510 --> 00:10:41.690
There doesn't seem to be a 
guest who could be a mother.

00:10:43.590 --> 00:10:45.490
Don't do that, Urinosuke.

00:10:46.050 --> 00:10:48.700
Looks like he's not interested in the baby.

00:10:48.700 --> 00:10:51.940
Urinosuke's totally settled in.

00:10:51.940 --> 00:10:53.750
I think that's fine.

00:10:53.750 --> 00:10:55.820
The boss hasn't said anything about it.

00:10:57.020 --> 00:10:59.950
Someone gave me this steamed bun 
while I was out on errands.

00:10:59.950 --> 00:11:02.390
I gave it to the baby, since it has teeth.

00:11:02.390 --> 00:11:05.350
All right, let's find its mother
while it's not crying.

00:11:13.860 --> 00:11:16.400
I bought thread and fabric.

00:11:19.060 --> 00:11:21.170
What a beautiful kimono.

00:11:21.170 --> 00:11:24.710
It's for a three-year-old's 
Shichi-Go-San celebration.

00:11:25.330 --> 00:11:27.810
I hope Shino will like it.

00:11:28.400 --> 00:11:29.760
<i>Shino-san?</i>

00:11:29.760 --> 00:11:31.380
<i>I wonder if that's her granddaughter.</i>

00:11:31.380 --> 00:11:37.830
Long ago, children were said to belong 
to the gods until they were seven.

00:11:38.140 --> 00:11:39.560
To the gods?

00:11:40.060 --> 00:11:44.600
They finally become human if 
they survive for seven years.

00:11:44.600 --> 00:11:47.710
That's what Shichi-Go-San celebrates.

00:11:48.510 --> 00:11:50.070
That's beautiful.

00:11:50.070 --> 00:11:52.490
I'm sure Shino-san will love it.

00:11:54.260 --> 00:11:55.380
Satsuki-chan.

00:11:55.380 --> 00:11:56.930
Where did that baby go?

00:11:56.930 --> 00:11:59.820
I took my eyes off of it for a 
brief moment, and now it's gone.

00:12:00.510 --> 00:12:03.640
I'm sure the mother 
found it and took it back.

00:12:03.640 --> 00:12:06.030
I hope that's what happened.

00:12:07.280 --> 00:12:09.770
Did something just pass by?

00:12:16.570 --> 00:12:18.600
First a baby, and now a lost kid?!

00:12:18.600 --> 00:12:20.210
Wait, Satsuki-chan.

00:12:21.080 --> 00:12:21.830
That kimono...

00:12:22.760 --> 00:12:25.000
Her name is Shino-chan.

00:12:25.000 --> 00:12:28.180
I just spoke with her grandmother.

00:12:28.560 --> 00:12:30.510
That's a relief.

00:12:31.020 --> 00:12:32.580
Let's take her...

00:12:35.800 --> 00:12:38.080
Damn it! Today is cursed.

00:12:38.070 --> 00:12:39.400
Mommy?

00:12:39.420 --> 00:12:42.150
I don't remember giving birth to you.

00:12:43.760 --> 00:12:46.660
Don't make her cry, Satsuki-chan.

00:12:46.660 --> 00:12:48.140
I-I didn't!

00:12:48.140 --> 00:12:49.950
Shino-chan, come over—

00:12:51.990 --> 00:12:53.360
<i>Merlion!</i>

00:12:55.380 --> 00:12:57.700
Oh, good... She's laughing.

00:13:09.890 --> 00:13:12.720
You can wear this yukata 
until your kimono is dry.

00:13:16.010 --> 00:13:16.890
Shino-chan!

00:13:17.330 --> 00:13:18.390
Bye!

00:13:19.090 --> 00:13:20.730
Don't you "Bye" me.

00:13:20.730 --> 00:13:22.720
Damn it, she's making so much work for me.

00:13:24.430 --> 00:13:29.230
<i>Satsuki-chan's smile is so adorable.</i>

00:13:30.100 --> 00:13:32.060
What are you grinning about?

00:13:32.060 --> 00:13:33.710
Nothing!

00:13:35.040 --> 00:13:37.240
My, Shino.

00:13:37.240 --> 00:13:39.640
Where did you leave your kimono?

00:13:40.870 --> 00:13:43.470
Whatever shall I do with you?

00:13:44.800 --> 00:13:47.020
It's so nice out.

00:13:49.690 --> 00:13:51.400
What are you up to?

00:13:52.530 --> 00:13:55.550
Oh, your ball's stuck in the tree.

00:14:00.310 --> 00:14:02.640
You can't be <i>too</i> rambunctious.

00:14:08.960 --> 00:14:11.870
You're going to get your 
pretty kimono all dirty.

00:14:13.650 --> 00:14:14.860
Um...

00:14:16.070 --> 00:14:20.240
Th-Thank you, Onii-chan.

00:14:23.420 --> 00:14:25.910
I'm an onee-chan, actually.

00:14:28.050 --> 00:14:31.760
My, what's the matter, Shino?

00:14:32.300 --> 00:14:35.090
Do you want to grow up faster?

00:14:36.000 --> 00:14:37.570
Sure.

00:14:37.560 --> 00:14:41.310
I'll make you a furisode next,

00:14:41.610 --> 00:14:45.110
so that you can grow up 
to be a lovely lady soon.

00:14:48.760 --> 00:14:51.200
Why are you crying?

00:14:52.900 --> 00:14:56.160
My mother made me a furisode.

00:14:56.160 --> 00:14:58.280
Oh, that's great.

00:14:58.280 --> 00:15:01.620
But my mom's taste in fashion is so old!

00:15:01.960 --> 00:15:04.040
I don't want to wear this!

00:15:08.190 --> 00:15:09.260
How's that?

00:15:09.260 --> 00:15:11.070
You can't just complain.

00:15:11.070 --> 00:15:14.420
You're a girl. You have to think 
of your own ways to be stylish.

00:15:14.420 --> 00:15:18.640
Do you think I can become 
pretty like you, Onee-chan?

00:15:18.640 --> 00:15:20.430
Wh-What are you talking about?

00:15:20.430 --> 00:15:22.660
I-I suppose you could.

00:15:22.660 --> 00:15:24.100
Maybe not <i>as</i> pretty as me.

00:15:24.490 --> 00:15:27.310
Ren, have you seen my pajamas?

00:15:27.610 --> 00:15:30.210
The ones you tossed on the floor?

00:15:30.210 --> 00:15:32.890
I washed them for you, since you never will.

00:15:33.450 --> 00:15:36.220
That's my Ren! You're so kind!

00:15:36.640 --> 00:15:38.420
N-Natsume, you idiot!

00:15:38.420 --> 00:15:40.470
People are watching!

00:15:40.470 --> 00:15:41.210
Huh?

00:15:41.760 --> 00:15:43.410
She's gone.

00:15:43.410 --> 00:15:44.980
Who was that girl?

00:15:44.980 --> 00:15:46.270
I don't know.

00:15:46.270 --> 00:15:47.880
She's probably a guest's child.

00:15:48.280 --> 00:15:50.700
<i>I wonder if she's her older sister.</i>

00:15:56.780 --> 00:15:59.000
Pardon me, ma'am.

00:15:59.540 --> 00:16:01.970
I brought thread and fabric.

00:16:02.240 --> 00:16:04.490
Come in, Onee-san.

00:16:05.710 --> 00:16:08.190
I'm sorry it's such a mess here.

00:16:08.190 --> 00:16:10.380
I'll go make some tea.

00:16:09.630 --> 00:16:11.600
Um, I...

00:16:12.030 --> 00:16:14.560
Another new kimono?

00:16:14.560 --> 00:16:17.800
That's right, Mother.

00:16:18.310 --> 00:16:23.080
Shino grows so fast, I can't keep up.

00:16:24.030 --> 00:16:26.460
She's going through her growth spurt.

00:16:26.690 --> 00:16:30.290
It seems she's fallen in love, too.

00:16:30.650 --> 00:16:35.210
Oh, don't tell Jirou-san about this.

00:16:35.780 --> 00:16:38.950
That man is so attached to his children.

00:16:39.290 --> 00:16:42.100
He'll become jealous, I'm sure.

00:16:42.430 --> 00:16:44.510
Right, Shino?

00:16:46.570 --> 00:16:50.200
This is our secret, right?

00:16:54.990 --> 00:16:56.440
Excuse me.

00:16:58.620 --> 00:17:02.670
Yuzu, you were raised 
by humans, weren't you?

00:17:03.740 --> 00:17:04.560
Yes.

00:17:05.790 --> 00:17:08.030
Then have you heard about this tradition?

00:17:08.400 --> 00:17:11.270
A mother who'd lost her daughter young

00:17:11.270 --> 00:17:14.810
would dress a doll in wedding 
clothes in her place,

00:17:15.350 --> 00:17:18.230
so that the daughter would 
marry in the afterlife.

00:17:18.510 --> 00:17:21.130
What do you think, Yuzu?

00:17:22.820 --> 00:17:28.440
Do you feel sorry for that lady, 
spending time with people who aren't here?

00:17:30.700 --> 00:17:38.030
If that's what the guest wants, 
then the world she sees is the true world.

00:17:38.840 --> 00:17:42.350
Guests are gods, after all.

00:17:50.790 --> 00:17:52.640
What's the matter?

00:17:52.640 --> 00:17:54.450
You look down.

00:17:54.450 --> 00:17:56.080
There you are, you tanuki.

00:17:57.500 --> 00:17:59.380
I'm not a tanuki.

00:17:59.380 --> 00:18:00.420
I'm a fox.

00:18:00.420 --> 00:18:02.330
I don't care either way.

00:18:02.330 --> 00:18:04.380
Stop deceiving my mom, please.

00:18:04.840 --> 00:18:07.340
You're in your rebellious phase.

00:18:07.340 --> 00:18:10.600
You couldn't have chosen a more 
complicated age for a human to be.

00:18:10.810 --> 00:18:14.200
When are you going to set 
her free from this place?

00:18:15.260 --> 00:18:17.150
<b>Konohanatei</b>

00:18:17.490 --> 00:18:22.800
Our guest came through our 
entrance of her own free will.

00:18:23.240 --> 00:18:25.460
I can't kick her out.

00:18:26.210 --> 00:18:30.390
Why don't you enjoy your time here, too?

00:18:30.390 --> 00:18:31.680
How can I?

00:18:32.000 --> 00:18:34.210
This is all a dream.

00:18:34.210 --> 00:18:37.100
You're just going to make her even 
more miserable when she wakes up!

00:18:37.100 --> 00:18:38.730
But, young lady,

00:18:40.310 --> 00:18:43.240
the fleeting dreams you have
here at Konohanatei,

00:18:43.240 --> 00:18:46.010
the entirety of your human lives...

00:18:46.330 --> 00:18:49.690
To us foxes, it's not much different.

00:18:50.600 --> 00:18:53.040
"Ah, what a nice dream that was."

00:18:53.040 --> 00:18:54.680
Isn't that good enough?

00:18:55.310 --> 00:18:59.610
At the very least, our guest 
doesn't mind that it's a dream.

00:19:03.990 --> 00:19:07.200
Don't tell anyone what I just said.

00:19:08.980 --> 00:19:13.870
I keep embarrassing myself 
in front of the people here.

00:19:14.620 --> 00:19:18.970
That's what it means 
for a person to grow up.

00:19:19.800 --> 00:19:23.450
Embarrass yourself often, 
regret all kinds of things,

00:19:23.900 --> 00:19:28.580
and please, become a beautiful woman.

00:19:30.200 --> 00:19:32.450
She's such a pretty bride.

00:19:32.700 --> 00:19:34.600
Which room is she staying in?

00:19:34.900 --> 00:19:37.060
The Kasumi room.

00:19:41.150 --> 00:19:44.030
Are you all right, little attendant?

00:19:48.080 --> 00:19:49.370
Thank you.

00:19:52.870 --> 00:19:57.260
Her final kimono was finished this morning.

00:19:58.360 --> 00:20:00.970
What a nice day.

00:20:01.710 --> 00:20:04.810
A perfectly clear spring sky.

00:20:05.450 --> 00:20:08.650
Just like the day you were born.

00:20:09.740 --> 00:20:13.610
You look beautiful, Shino.

00:20:14.830 --> 00:20:18.260
You said I was the child of a god.

00:20:19.140 --> 00:20:22.300
But I've always been your daughter.

00:20:23.250 --> 00:20:27.730
I've lived a truly fulfilling, dream-like life.

00:20:29.360 --> 00:20:30.660
Thank you,

00:20:32.770 --> 00:20:34.140
mother.

00:20:45.320 --> 00:20:48.060
Thank you, miss.

00:20:48.330 --> 00:20:53.800
The attendants have helped me feel 
very happy during my time here.

00:20:53.800 --> 00:20:56.820
It truly was like a dream.

00:20:56.820 --> 00:20:58.740
It wasn't a dream.

00:21:00.200 --> 00:21:04.370
You'll always be with 
your daughter from now on.

00:21:04.690 --> 00:21:09.280
For much longer than the few decades 
that you've been kept apart.

00:21:14.470 --> 00:21:20.300
What a wonderful day today is.

00:21:23.420 --> 00:21:26.870
Lunch is served, ma'am.

00:21:32.630 --> 00:21:35.370
Our guest has just departed.

00:21:35.720 --> 00:21:37.810
To where her daughter awaits.

00:21:37.810 --> 00:21:39.320
Really?

00:21:39.640 --> 00:21:42.120
She must have been in a hurry.

00:21:42.120 --> 00:21:45.530
I'm a little disappointed 
that I couldn't see her off.

00:21:45.930 --> 00:21:48.740
Speaking of which, she wanted to thank us.

00:21:49.340 --> 00:21:53.610
She said the past few days 
were like a dream, thanks to us.

00:21:57.790 --> 00:22:00.160
Now, then, we have a banquet tonight.

00:22:00.160 --> 00:22:01.620
It's going to be a huge job, Yuzu.

00:22:01.620 --> 00:22:02.600
Be ready!

00:22:02.600 --> 00:22:03.360
Yes!

00:23:35.010 --> 00:23:39.970
<b>Next Episode: 
The Spring Rains Bring With It</b>
